\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\f0\fs22\lang9 1. Objective \f1\emdash  Business / Functional View\par
\par
T\b0 he objective of the Root Cause Analysis (RCA) solution is to provide an intelligent, automated investigation capability that can identify application incidents, gather relevant evidence from multiple operational systems, compare the current problem with historical incidents, and produce a reasoned root-cause assessment. Rather than requiring support teams to manually search logs, source-code changes, deployments, previous incidents, and troubleshooting records, the solution uses an AI model and an agent to coordinate the investigation.\par
\par
AI Model and Agent involvement: An AI model performs the reasoning and correlation, while an AI agent orchestrates the investigation. When an abnormal application event occurs, the agent receives the incident context, determines what additional information is required, selects the appropriate information sources, evaluates the returned evidence, and continues investigating until it has enough information to produce an RCA.\par
The solution combines current operational evidence with historical organizational knowledge. Historical incidents, previous errors, resolutions, and troubleshooting information help determine whether the current issue resembles something that has occurred before.\par
Current engineering information such as source-code commits, merge requests, approvals, builds, releases, deployments, and job logs can be retrieved during an investigation to determine whether a recent change is related to the incident.\par
Incident-management information can also be examined to identify related incidents, their current status, previous resolutions, assignment information, and supporting attachments.\par
The desired outcome is an RCA containing the probable cause, supporting evidence, related historical incidents or changes, confidence in the conclusion, and recommended next actions. Once sufficient confidence is reached, the solution can subsequently automate operational actions such as creating a ticket or notifying support teams.\f0\par
